  {
   "approach": "Park in the large lot at Horseshoe Lake, at the end of Highway 203, and hike the Mammoth Pass Trail as far as McLeod Lake. Work around the lake shore to its southwest side, where a well-worn path enters the trees, then follow the use trail that climbs the hillside beside a talus slide to the snowfield and talus band beneath the walls of the crest; snow can linger there into summer. The route is the left of the two fully bolted lines on the Ski Tracks Wall.",
   "area_id": "ca_mammoth_crest",
   "descent": null,
