  {
   "approach": "Park in the large lot at Horseshoe Lake, at the end of Highway 203, and hike the Mammoth Pass Trail as far as McLeod Lake. Work around the lake shore to its southwest side, where a well-worn path enters the trees, then follow the use trail that climbs the hillside beside a talus slide to the snowfield and talus band beneath the walls of the crest; snow can linger there into summer. The route is well left of the Requiem Wall, on the right side of an obvious class 2 gully that leads to the rim, beside a big tree; stay low on the approach until directly below the gully.",
